WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.099 --> 00:00:07.270
The true conflict of One Punch Man is Saitama's
hopeless obsession for just another fun fight,

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:10.930
and his refusal to move on with his life from
that.

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:15.380
Saitama keeps saying that he is a hero for
fun. And yet, if there is one thing we know

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:21.630
about the strongest anime character ever,
it's that he doesn't have a lot of fun being

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:33.429
one. The guy who right from the start has
everything, that all other shounen heroes

00:00:33.429 --> 00:00:39.210
dream of and desperately struggle for, is
suffering from a dreadful existential crisis

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:44.920
because how this power. But I feel like people
are surprisingly confused about the POINT

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:50.510
One Punch man is trying to make as a story.
It's not merely a parody of conventional shounen

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:55.421
and superheroes stories, or merely a story
about what it means to be a good hero. It's

00:00:55.421 --> 00:01:02.889
also one that you will find has surprisingly
deep and profound views on life and happiness

00:01:02.889 --> 00:01:13.100
and purpose. I learned that One Punch man
is such a masterpiece because it resonates

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:17.250
with you on not one, but exactly 4 levels
of meaning.

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:19.329
Level 1: The Parody.

00:01:19.329 --> 00:01:23.759
Saitama is fucking hilarious. If you ever
watched any of my videos, you'll know that

00:01:23.759 --> 00:01:30.420
I absolutely love Shounen Anime. The epic
fights, the tragic backstories, the inspiring

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:35.990
training arcs, the mentor guy with the white
hair who is cooler than the main character,

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:41.689
I love it all. The problem you might have
realized, is that this description basically

00:01:41.689 --> 00:01:48.580
fits every single anime out there. And now
we have to things we don't want, predictability

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:50.680
and repetitiveness.

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:55.939
What made One Punch man an instant success,
even with the first episode, is that it brutally

00:01:55.939 --> 00:02:01.590
makes fun of the typical hero. Hell, the name
of the Anime itself is a parody. One Punch

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:08.100
Man, a guy who defeats any enemy in an instant,
starts with the hero, where all other stories

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:13.350
end, at the pinnacle of the world, the strongest
of them all. And it's usually the story of

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:18.550
how we got there, that is so exciting. All
the blood and tears that were shed along the

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:24.030
way. All the obstacles and enemies that had
to be overcome and all the relationships formed

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:30.250
along the way. All of it to become the strongest
in order to change the world. Saitama is a

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:38.760
guy who used to work at a convenience store,
who then decided to become a hero for fun.

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:44.190
He didn't have any major motivation and the
most struggle he went through was doing a

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:51.070
basic daily work-out routine. Well that and
loosing his hair. But at the start of the

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:56.210
story, he is pretty much an average guy, who
got sort of motivated to do something great

00:02:56.210 --> 00:03:01.980
but actually succeeded right away. And for
anyone who has suffered through the endless

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:07.410
training-arcs and dead loved ones dies so
I guess you get a power up scenes, this is

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:10.110
just a hilarious thing so see.

00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:15.030
The true magic however, lies in the fact,
that every single character in One Punch man

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:23.420
is written as 100% serious. EXCEPT Saitama.
Everyone is designed to fit perfectly into

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:29.520
your typical anime trope. Genos, Garou and
Mumen Rider are text-book example of SHounen

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:40.130
protagonists, all with their own struggles
and the will to become stronger. With Bang,

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:47.340
you have the powerful wise mentor and pretty
much every single villain, whether minor or

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:55.120
major, would fit perfectly as a serious opponent
in any other story. All the characters have

00:03:55.120 --> 00:04:03.400
cool designs, tragic pasts and complex motivations.
Everyone is drawn seriously and acts seriously.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:11.220
EXCEPT Saitama. He's a pretty boring, average
dude, that is purposefully lazily and comically

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:16.320
drawn. And yet, since he is the strongest
of them all, he stomps on the accomplishments

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:18.630
of all the serious characters around him.

00:04:18.630 --> 00:04:23.510
Take for instance Mumen rider, who's courage
in the face of an enemy that out-matches him

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:35.070
completely. We see him suffer and still get
up again and again, proving all the qualities

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:40.970
we want in our typical hero. I got so excited
for him defeating the enemy against all odds.

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:46.960
But, Just when you feel that hard work and
true grit will pay off Mumen rider is defeated

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:53.620
in a single punch and it is no other than
Saitama who arrives to effortlessly save the

00:04:53.620 --> 00:05:06.530
day, thinking to himself [...]. 
The character I identify with gets defeated

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:13.840
in an instant, while all my hopes are undercut
by one effortless punch. It's so funny, because

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:17.850
I know exactly that the Anime is making fun
of my expectations.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:23.380
And I realized that the same happens with
villains as well. Dr. Genus, exiled from the

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:36.780
scientific community he spends fifty years
trying to unlock the key to humanity’s evolution,

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:42.330
finally creating the powerful and mentally
unstable creature, Carnage Kabuto. A creature

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:49.230
fully taken in by his own power and perfection.
And yet all this buildup and characterization

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:56.410
for both of these antagonists is once again
undercut right away. When Kabuto gets Saitama

00:05:56.410 --> 00:06:02.870
to reveal&nbsp;the secret behind his power, usually
an opportunity to depict a character’s mental

00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:15.770
and physical development, it turns out to
be a simple workout routine. [...] The 

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:22.150
ease with which he reached the top and defeats
all enemies, robbs all the supporting characters,

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:25.830
like Genos of any meaning they’ve derived
from their struggles.

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:31.750
The rate at which One Punch man keeps subverting
common Anime and Superhero tropes is pure

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:40.010
greatness. Saitama has ungodly power and the
worst or I guess best part is he didn’t

00:06:40.010 --> 00:06:45.840
do anything special to deserve it, he isn’t
the chosen one or the underdog who sacrificed

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:51.620
everything to get to the top, he really is
just a twenty five year old guy who’s unsatisfied

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:58.570
with work. And I laugh my ass off every single
episode as a result of this. Let's go to level

00:06:58.570 --> 00:06:59.570
2.

00:06:59.570 --> 00:07:00.570
But first Ad Break.

