00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:37.889
Level 2: The social critique.

00:07:37.889 --> 00:07:43.940
Shounen is predictable, obsession corrupts
and life without a challenge is pointless.

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:47.800
Once I started to dig a little bit deeper
into the comedic surface of One Punch man,

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:52.800
I quickly discovered that many aspects of
the Anime are quite critical of the current

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:58.940
state of shounen anime, the concept of superheroes
and the societies these stories take place

00:07:58.940 --> 00:07:59.940
in.

00:07:59.940 --> 00:08:04.340
The first and most obvious message I found
is once again directly connected to the premise

00:08:04.340 --> 00:08:17.330
of the story. Saitama is a man who has obtained
absolute power. He is the strongest and able

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:23.140
to defeat one end-boss level monster after
the next. Something every other Hero dedicates

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:27.979
his entire being towards. And yet, at the
end of it all, he is as dissatisfied as he

00:08:27.979 --> 00:08:37.079
was working a regular job. Life is dull without
a challenge. When there are no stakes and

00:08:37.079 --> 00:08:42.849
no consequences to fear for anything we do,
life becomes less enjoyable. Beginning the

00:08:42.849 --> 00:08:48.089
story as a disillusioned young man with a
full head of hair searching for a job in business,

00:08:48.089 --> 00:08:53.499
he discovers a passion for hero work that,
for the first time in his life, lights a fire

00:08:53.499 --> 00:08:58.709
in his eyes. But three years later, the thrill
is gone, along with this his trademark anime

00:08:58.709 --> 00:09:03.959
hair and he has gained the power to end any
fight in just one punch. Even though Saitama

00:09:03.959 --> 00:09:09.519
is a really nice guy, he has fallen prey to
his own desires and expectations. After all,

00:09:09.519 --> 00:09:15.699
his desire to become a hero in the first place
was because he thought it was fun, finally

00:09:15.699 --> 00:09:26.970
he could be good at. Even though he usually
does the morally right thing, he doesn't fight

00:09:26.970 --> 00:09:33.240
to safe others, but for his own pleasure.
And since he is already the strongest, this

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:40.040
obsession with having a good fight, leaves
him eternal dissatisfied. That is the true

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:43.350
conflict in One Punch Man.

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:51.490
It's a central theme of the story. Becoming
obsessed with the goal of becoming stronger,

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:56.779
which typically sets our hero apart from the
rest and allows him to grow, is explored through

00:09:56.779 --> 00:10:01.730
a more human and realistic lens here.
Take a moment to appreciate that the most

00:10:01.730 --> 00:10:07.740
common way normal people turn into Monsters
in this world is by succumbing to their obsessions:

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:13.399
Crablante, for example, was so obsessed with
eating crabs that he turned into one. Phoenix

00:10:13.399 --> 00:10:18.649
Man was obsessed with grief and with his role
in his cancelled TV show, so much that he

00:10:18.649 --> 00:10:26.170
merged with his bird costume. Genos and turns
less and less human with every upgrade he

00:10:26.170 --> 00:10:35.959
gets. Just as Garou becomes more and more
Monster, the harder he pushes. All the way

00:10:35.959 --> 00:10:42.139
to Amai Mask, who is consumed by his desire
to be beautiful. I got the strong feeling,

00:10:42.139 --> 00:10:47.610
that the lines between Humans and monsters
get more and more blurred as the story unfolds.

00:10:47.610 --> 00:10:53.550
So, once again subverting typical Anime tropes,
the main theme is not about not giving up.

00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:59.649
In fact, the story has made it clear that
there are times when a person should give

00:10:59.649 --> 00:11:03.269
up. It's about staying human.

00:11:03.269 --> 00:11:13.290
That insight really hit home for me when I
rewatched the last episode of season one.

00:11:13.290 --> 00:11:19.429
Boros' backstory is actually the exact same
as Saitamas. He is an invincible being that

00:11:19.429 --> 00:11:25.319
got so obsessed with a good fight, that he
started eradicating planets in order to find

00:11:25.319 --> 00:11:32.360
strong opponents. He is a mirror for Saitama's
fault. A warning for what our bald hero might

00:11:32.360 --> 00:11:35.720
become, should he find no way to leave his
obsession behind.

00:11:35.720 --> 00:11:40.050
On a larger scale, I also found that One Punch
man also criticizes the concepts of superhero

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:44.920
societies in general. How do creators keep
on upping the stakes and make it interesting

00:11:44.920 --> 00:11:49.820
for fans who’ve already seen it all? Is
there a point where it all starts to feel

00:11:49.820 --> 00:11:54.999
recycled? In the world of One Punch man, this
is expressed in form of the Hero association,

00:11:54.999 --> 00:12:06.730
who's creation was actually sparked by Saitama
when he saved the little kid form the crab.

00:12:06.730 --> 00:12:11.459
As it turns out daddy had a lot of money.
However, since Saitama lives outside the system,

00:12:11.459 --> 00:12:16.769
we get to experience it for the first time
side by side with him. I found that the Hero

00:12:16.769 --> 00:12:22.249
Association's ranking system and the egos
and internal strife within it are an interesting

00:12:22.249 --> 00:12:29.629
take on the idea of superheroes as famous
celebrities. Power doesn't corrupt, it reveals

00:12:29.629 --> 00:12:30.810
who you were all along.

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:31.810
This show was actually pretty serious in its
undertone and mercilessly deconstructs some

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:32.810
of the issues often ignored in Anime.

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:34.070
Level 3: The life lesson.

00:12:34.070 --> 00:12:38.829
Saitama teaches you what actually matters
in life. You may or may not believe me, but

00:12:38.829 --> 00:12:45.829
the true message behind One punch man actually
goes even deeper. Far from being a pure comedy

00:12:45.829 --> 00:12:51.119
show or simply criticizing the status quo
in anime, One has intentionally planned his

00:12:51.119 --> 00:12:56.489
story to be the real deal right from the start.
The world of One Punch man with its enormous

00:12:56.489 --> 00:13:02.829
cities that are harassed by cataclysmic monsters
every other day, is built specifically for

00:13:02.829 --> 00:13:07.589
Saitama to work as the protagonist. A guy
who punches big and strong things on a daily

00:13:07.589 --> 00:13:13.120
basis. That makes it even more impressive
than to me, how rich and real this world starts

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:18.660
to feel a few episodes into the story. I talked
about all characters but Saitama being written

00:13:18.660 --> 00:13:24.290
completely seiriously. But that does not only
result in a comedic effect, it also makes

00:13:24.290 --> 00:13:29.430
these people feel real and relatable and we
have a lot of fantastic character arcs for

00:13:29.430 --> 00:13:37.839
people like Genos, Garo or Sonic.

00:13:37.839 --> 00:13:42.739
Their contrast to Saitama is not only to be
funny, they contrast him to shine light on

00:13:42.739 --> 00:13:45.610
the true point of One Punch man as a story.
Saitama is purposefully created as the exact

00:13:45.610 --> 00:13:49.290
opposite of an anime protagonist. Drawing
him as simply as he is has the really fascinating

00:13:49.290 --> 00:13:55.500
effect, that we have to judge him not by his
appearance, but by his actions and personality.

00:13:55.500 --> 00:14:01.829
No epic hair and no badass costume. Saitama
is so special as a main character because

00:14:01.829 --> 00:14:05.339
people love him for just himself.

00:14:05.339 --> 00:14:11.029
Wanting to be the strongest, is something
that only very few people relate to. Worrying

00:14:11.029 --> 00:14:18.259
about money, what to have for dinner and procrastinating
stuff on the other hand: Relatable. Watching

00:14:18.259 --> 00:14:24.040
TV and playing video games on a Tuesday morning?
Also Extremely Relatable.

00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:29.860
Saitama is easy to love as a character because
power reveals who someone is at heart. And

00:14:29.860 --> 00:14:35.420
Saitama is just this nice, but kind of clueless
dude in his 20s. And it's no big surprise

00:14:35.420 --> 00:14:46.709
I think that this is attractive.

00:14:46.709 --> 00:14:50.929
Most importantly however, Saitama's big flaw
as a character might be the most relatable

00:14:50.929 --> 00:14:55.799
thing of them all. He is obsessed with the
thought that being a strong hero will make

00:14:55.799 --> 00:15:02.900
him happy. Will fulfill him. And yet once
he gets what he wants, it doesn't. The real

00:15:02.900 --> 00:15:07.550
journey of Saitama is not to find someone
that he can have a real fight with. Once that's

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:14.069
over it would be just straight back to dissatisfaction.
It's Saitama realizing that he needs to move

00:15:14.069 --> 00:15:19.989
on from his fantasy and actually becoming
a great hero character-wise. Finding happiness

00:15:19.989 --> 00:15:24.899
in the moment by spending time with people
like Genos and finding purpose in his ability

00:15:24.899 --> 00:15:31.350
to protect humanity and inspire others. It
is actually King, who summarizes the goal

00:15:31.350 --> 00:15:39.619
of One punch man perfectly: ["You are the
most powerful hero of all, BUT you are NOT

00:15:39.619 --> 00:15:47.769
the best hero, aspire to be one."]. Here is
another video for you to watch!

